// DRAFT (Act III, planning only). Ch17 B12 "Hollowmere at work" (P, 6 min): field barks, kind and practical
// (act3_ch17.md §2 B02, B12). The tally hull's record-keeper (Ch15's clerk) nods to Toma (ch15_toma_on_the_tally); the lookout bark is the only sign
// of the Order's patrols (§10 Q5). Tobin's absence is felt, never explained. One node per bark.
title: ch17_bark_lookout
location: ch17/hollowmere
---
Hull_captain as "Lookout" [neutral]: Nothing on the water but us. I'll call it if that changes. #line:ch17_bark_001
===
title: ch17_bark_tally_keeper
---
<<if $ch15_toma_on_the_tally>>
    @anim clerk nod toma
    Clerk as "Record-keeper" [neutral]: Your name's where you asked. Under the camp. Nobody's crossed it out. #line:ch17_bark_002
<<else>>
    Clerk as "Record-keeper" [neutral]: Every camp that burned, written down. Somebody has to keep the list. #line:ch17_bark_003
<<endif>>
===
title: ch17_bark_chandler
---
Vendor as "Chandler" [neutral]: Oil, rope, glass. Tobin used to fetch the glass. Take what you need. #line:ch17_bark_004
===
title: ch17_bark_pell_windmills
---
Pell [neutral]: They turn with nobody singing to them. I like that. #line:ch17_bark_005
===
title: ch17_bark_ysolde_asleep
---
@anim ysolde sleep_over keth_cord
Liss [soft_smile]: Leave her. She's been at it since dawn. #line:ch17_bark_006
===
